  "body": "Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), briefs q04 and q06, CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release with SolidCraft **v0.46.2**; reproduced by hand.\n\n## What happens\n\nSolidCraft's `sketch.export_dxf` (with `join: true`, LWPOLYLINE output) and `file.export_view_dxf` write AC1015 DXF files that contain a `CLASSES` section (lines 46-49 of the file below). CamCraft refuses the whole file:\n\n```\nimport_dxf {\"name\": \"L\", \"path\": \".../q04-vcarve-sign-letters.dxf\", \"units\": \"mm\"}\n-> import_dxf: DXF import: DXF CLASSES: unsupported SECTION\n```\n\n`crates/geometry/src/dxf/reader.rs` on main still reads only HEADER, ENTITIES, TABLES, BLOCKS and OBJECTS and errors on any other section name. CLASSES is a standard section of every AC1015+ DXF (it carries no geometry). The agents' workaround was to export R12 LINE entities (`join: false`), which imported (894 lines, 2 closed chains).\n\n## Expected\n\nA CLASSES section (and THUMBNAILIMAGE, ACDSDATA) is skipped and the entities import.\n\n## Repro files\n\n[q04-vcarve-sign-letters.dxf](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/q04-vcarve-sign-letters.dxf) (refused), [q04-vcarve-sign-letters-r12.dxf](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/q04-vcarve-sign-letters-r12.dxf) (same letters, imports), [q06-die-lines.dxf](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q06-wire-plasma/q06-die-lines.dxf) (export_view_dxf, refused).\n\nDone means: q04-vcarve-sign-letters.dxf imports with the same 2 closed chains as the R12 file (pinned by a reader test with a CLASSES section).\n",
